      "id": 18,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Policy history stays in the product\nPostgres persists **normalized policy snapshots** and sync-run evidence; **`/api/v1/policies` `history.recent_snapshots` and `history.comparison_to_previous`** (including source-readiness posture and per-snapshot counts) are the **product contract** for how that persisted slice evolved.\n\nThis Grafana dashboard does **not** replay persisted snapshot timelines or comparisons. It shows **current** metrics only (counts, shares, labels, sync age).\n\nWhat Grafana panels here **do** show:\n- policy counts and collection health\n- bounded static-policy detail gaps versus observed policy counts where metrics expose them\n- detail-ready target **share** as a **current** observability mirror—not a persisted-history or drift verdict\n- live-empty / detail-unavailable / partial-detail **flags** as **current** posture mirrors—per-target reasons stay on the Policies page\n- persisted policy sync age, counts, and result posture as **sync** observability, not policy workflow state\n\nOperators who need **history** (anchors, comparison, how source-readiness moved across snapshots) should use the **Policies page** and the API; `./scripts/verify-core-runtime.sh` conditionally asserts those JSON keys when Postgres holds policy snapshot rows.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Policy history is product-owned",
      "type": "text"
    },
